You are correct; it is not "mandatory" for segment length to be twice truncation distance.  Covariates (if remotely sensed) usually come as pixels that are more or less square.  Likewise when constructing a prediction grid, as is done for prediction with density surface modelling, the prediction grid cells are usually square.  It is sensible for the segments and prediction grid components to have similar shapes.

